<%# Google AdSense slot.

    Renders NOTHING unless both are true:
      1. ADSENSE_CLIENT is set (ca-pub-…), and
      2. the visitor has given consent for advertising cookies.

    Both gates are deliberate, and the second is not optional politeness.
    brgen serves Norway, so every visitor is in the EEA. Google requires a
    Consent Management Platform certified against IAB TCF v2.2 before it will
    serve ads to EEA/UK traffic at all — without one, requests are answered
    with blank ads, and serving personalised ads without a consent signal is a
    GDPR violation regardless of what Google does.

    There is no CMP in this app yet. `advertising_consent?` therefore returns
    false for everyone, so this partial is inert by construction: it can be
    placed on surfaces now and will start serving only once a CMP is wired and
    actually records a choice. Defaulting the other way — render the script,
    fix consent later — is how sites end up serving unconsented ads for months.

    Locals:
      slot   — AdSense ad slot id (required to render)
      layout — "auto" (default), "in-article", "in-feed"
%>
<% slot = local_assigns[:slot].to_s %>
<% client = ENV["ADSENSE_CLIENT"].to_s %>
<% if client.present? && slot.present? && advertising_consent? %>
  <aside class="ad-slot" aria-label="<%= t("shared.advertisement") %>">
    <%# Labelled, because an unlabelled ad next to real listings is
        indistinguishable from editorial content. %>
    <p class="ad-slot-label"><%= t("shared.advertisement") %></p>
    <ins class="adsbygoogle"
         style="display:block" <%# scan: intentional — AdSense requires the inline display %>
         data-ad-client="<%= client %>"
         data-ad-slot="<%= slot %>"
         data-ad-format="<%= local_assigns.fetch(:layout, "auto") %>"
         data-full-width-responsive="true"></ins>
  </aside>
<% end %>
